From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:58:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Mesa Venus generated Soong port

Describe the port with the Android.bp files tools/generate-mesa-venus-port.py
generates for arm64 and arm: the Venus Vulkan HAL and the Virgl EGL and GLES
libraries the Android EGL loader finds through ro.hardware.egl=kernarium, and
only the modules those four build from or link. Every other module is scoped
with a venus_ prefix.

The OpenGL command marshalling bakes in the pointer size, so each instruction
set generates its own copy and the library selects it by arch.

A flag only the arm64 platform sets is a select where Soong makes the property
configurable and an arch block where it does not (conlyflags is a plain list).

Soong refuses any Android.mk under a denylisted directory, and this port is
described entirely by generated Android.bp files. The removed makefile builds
nothing this product installs.

Meson compiles every C and C++ file with -D_FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64, which the
converter does not carry over. The defaults every compiled module uses add it
for arm, whose off_t would otherwise be 32 bits: the Venus renderer mmaps DRM
offsets above 4 GiB.
